+# Review Draft
+
+## Context
+
+The contributor branch-and-PR flow now has a repo-local helper at `scripts/pr_flow.py`.
+It creates branches from `main`, pushes the current contributor branch, verifies the remote
+branch exists, opens a GitHub pull request, and switches back to `main` only after the PR is
+merged.
+
+## Durable Rule Candidate
+
+Branch names for this workflow should use one of these dated forms:
+
+- `feature/YYYY_MM_DD_description`
+- `chore/YYYY_MM_DD_description`
+- `fix/YYYY_MM_DD_description`
+
+## Existing Memory Interaction
+
+`ai-wiki/workflows.md` already described the Branch And Merge Flow and mentioned the missing
+`scripts/pr_flow.py` helper, but its older example prefixes included `feat/...` and `docs/...`.
+The helper and `CONTRIBUTING.md` now use the requested `feature`, `chore`, and `fix` forms.
+
+## Reuse Assessment
+
+Keep this as a draft until a human decides whether to update the shared workflow note. The code
+and contributor docs are already aligned with the new branch naming rule.
